(A)+(B)  hp odd (Rédei, control) and the PARITY OF hc,  n = 3..6 exhaustive
==============================================================================
  n = 3  (8 tournaments)
     hp always ODD (Rédei control) : True
     hc parity   : even 6 (75.0%),  odd 2 (25.0%)
     hc mod 4    : {0: 6, 1: 2}
     among STRONG    : even 0, odd 2
     among NON-strong: even 6, odd 0
  n = 4  (64 tournaments)
     hp always ODD (Rédei control) : True
     hc parity   : even 40 (62.5%),  odd 24 (37.5%)
     hc mod 4    : {0: 40, 1: 24}
     among STRONG    : even 0, odd 24
     among NON-strong: even 40, odd 0
  n = 5  (1024 tournaments)
     hp always ODD (Rédei control) : True
     hc parity   : even 624 (60.9%),  odd 400 (39.1%)
     hc mod 4    : {0: 480, 1: 360, 2: 144, 3: 40}
     among STRONG    : even 144, odd 400
     among NON-strong: even 480, odd 0
